<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

Several panels sharing one region, one shown at a time.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/tabs)

<%= embed UI::TabsPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Tabs(default_value: "overview") do
  TabsList do
    TabsTrigger(value: "overview") { "Overview" }
    TabsTrigger(value: "activity") { "Activity" }
  end
  TabsContent(value: "overview") { render "overview" }
  TabsContent(value: "activity") { render "activity" }
end
```

Each `TabsTrigger` is matched to the `TabsContent` with the same `value:`. The selected tab and panel are rendered
on the server (the others' panels are `hidden`), so the page is right before JavaScript loads; the `ui--tabs`
controller then switches panels, slides the indicator and handles the keyboard. `variant:` (`:pill`, `:line`),
`size:` and `orientation:` are set on the root. To move between pages use [Navigation](<%= page_path(:navigation) %>).

